{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Make fat.</b> Some say the word השמן is a noun of action like הקטר יקטירון כיום (II Samuel 15), and likewise השע like להשע. This is impossible because of the word פן; rather it is all imperative. We know that the prophet has no power to make the heart fat — it is by His word, and there are many like it:" "<b>Turn.</b> From the root לא תשעינה (Isaiah 32:3), like the meaning of טח, and likewise the Aramaic Targum. It should have been on the pattern of הרף, but it changed because of the guttural letter, or it may be among the second [group] verbs that appear:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Resolved the source citation שמואל ב' ט\"ו as II Samuel 15.", 1 "Reading השתנה as 'changed/altered'; 'the guttural letter' likely refers to ע in the root."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:29.390135200Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}